<p><a name="fn1"></a>
              1. The sample is selected from among the largest banks in
              each Federal Reserve District. In the table, large banks
              are defined as those with total domestic assets of $20
              billion or more as of    December 31, 2016.    The combined assets
              of the  43  large banks totaled    $10.0 trillion, compared to
                $10.2 trillion for the entire panel of  72  banks, and    $14.2
              trillion for all domestically chartered, federally insured
              commercial banks. <a href="#fn1r">Return to text</a></p>


                 

